{
  "name": "PyAgentic",
  "tagline": "A declarative, type-safe Python framework for building LLM agents",
  "description": "## What it is\nPyAgentic lets you build sophisticated LLM agents using clean, class-based Python. You subclass `BaseAgent`, decorate methods as tools, and declare state, linked sub-agents, and dependencies as typed class fields — and the framework compiles all of that into provider tool schemas, Pydantic I/O models, and (optionally) a fully-typed HTTP API, with type safety end to end.\n\n## How it works\nThe heart of PyAgentic is the **`AgentMeta` metaclass**. At class-definition time it walks the MRO using C3 linearization (so agents can inherit from other agents and from `AgentExtension` mixins), then introspects your class:\n- `@tool` methods become `_ToolDefinition`s, with parameter schemas derived from Python type hints.\n- `State[T]` fields become a generated per-agent state model (and auto-generated `get_/set_` tools gated by `read`/`write` access).\n- Linked agents (fields typed as another `BaseAgent`/`Link[T]`) are registered so they can be invoked as tools.\n- `Depends[T]` and `MCPLink` fields are recorded for server-side injection and MCP wiring.\n\nFrom that introspection the metaclass **pre-builds Pydantic models** the rest of the system keys off: `__request_model__` (from your `__call__` signature), a recursive `__construct_model__` (the serializable constructor, nesting each linked agent's own construct model), `__response_model__`, a discriminated-union `__stream_event_model__` for SSE, and the state class. Knowing an agent's full I/O contract before it's ever instantiated is what makes the rest of the framework declarative.\n\n## Highlights\n- **Declarative, compiled class model** — a metaclass turns your class into tool schemas + Pydantic contracts; inheritance and mixins resolve via C3 linearization, and `__instructions__` can embed a parent's rendered prompt with `{{ super }}`.\n- **Type hints → tool schemas** — `_ToolDefinition` maps primitives, lists, and nested Pydantic models to JSON Schema, emitting OpenAI (`strict`) and Anthropic (strict + `additionalProperties: false`) tool specs from the same definition. Params can carry dynamic `ref`-based enums resolved from live state.\n- **Provider abstraction** — models are selected with a `provider::model` string that resolves through an `LLMProviders` enum to built-in OpenAI, Anthropic, and Gemini backends (capabilities like tool-calling / structured output are declared per provider and validated up front). A pre-configured provider instance can be passed instead, and the `LLMProvider` ABC makes custom/OpenAI-compatible endpoints pluggable.\n- **Async agentic loop** — `step()` streams every `LLMResponse`, `ToolResponse`, and final `AgentResponse`; tool and linked-agent calls in a turn run concurrently via `asyncio.as_completed`, bounded by `max_call_depth`. `run()` collapses the stream to the final response.\n- **Agent linking** — a linked agent appears to the LLM as a tool whose parameters are that agent's `__call__` signature. By default each invocation runs on an isolated `fork()` (fresh state, shared provider/deps/MCP clients); `shared=True` keeps one serialized instance.\n- **Persistent, policied state** — `State` fields survive across turns; direct `agent.field` access is transparently routed through the state object, and message/list policies (sliding window, compaction, tool eviction/clipping) compact context before each inference.\n- **Serve any agent** — `create_app`/`create_router` derive FastAPI routes (sessions, sync + SSE-streaming chat, state, and a `/schema` endpoint) directly from the metaclass-generated models, so the **OpenAPI spec is auto-generated and always in sync**. `Depends[T]` fields are injected by type and validated at build time. Optional per-agent **MCP** server mounting exposes agents over the Model Context Protocol, and a durable async **jobs** system (SQLite/WAL-backed, crash-recoverable) runs long tasks past client timeouts.\n- **Observability** — built-in tracing (`BasicTracer`, `LangfuseTracer`) spans inference, tool, and agent calls.\n\n## Install\n```bash\npip install pyagentic-core\n```\n\n## Stack\nPython 3.13+, Pydantic v2, Transitions (phase state machines), FastAPI + Uvicorn (optional API layer), FastMCP (MCP client/server), and the OpenAI / Anthropic / Google Generative AI SDKs. Docs built with MkDocs Material. MIT licensed.",
